---
import LegalLayout from "@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import Todo from "@/components/Todo.astro";
import { site } from "@/config/site";

const controller = site.legalName || site.name;
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Chalybe Steel collects, uses and protects personal data submitted through chalybesteel.com, and how to exercise your data protection rights."
  updated="11 November 2026"
>
  {!site.legalName && (
    <p>
      <Todo note="add legal entity name and registered address as data controller before collecting data at scale (GDPR Art. 13 controller identification)" />
    </p>
  )}

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    This website, chalybesteel.com, is operated by {controller}
    {site.address && site.address.length > 0 && <>, {site.address.join(", ")}</>}
    {site.registrationNo && <> (registration no. {site.registrationNo})</>}. {controller} is the
    controller of personal data collected through this website. For any question about this policy
    or your personal data, contact <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>We collect only the data you give us when you send an enquiry or request for quotation:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Contact details: name, company, country, email address and, optionally, phone number.</li>
    <li>
      Enquiry details: product requirements, quantities, delivery information, your message and any
      file you attach.
    </li>
    <li>
      Technical data needed to deliver and protect the website, such as IP address and browser
      information processed by our hosting and security providers.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    This website does not use advertising or tracking cookies. If we add privacy-friendly analytics
    in future, we will update this policy before doing so.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use it and why</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      To respond to your enquiry, prepare quotations and take steps at your request before entering
      into a contract (legal basis: pre-contractual steps, GDPR Art. 6(1)(b)).
    </li>
    <li>
      To keep business correspondence and records, and to protect the website against abuse and spam
      (legal basis: our legitimate interests, Art. 6(1)(f)).
    </li>
    <li>
      To meet legal, tax and export-control obligations (legal basis: legal obligation, Art.
      6(1)(c)).
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell personal data or use it for automated decision-making.</p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We share personal data only where necessary to handle your enquiry or order:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Service providers that host this website, protect it from abuse and deliver email on our
      behalf.
    </li>
    <li>
      Manufacturers, inspection agencies and logistics providers, where needed to prepare a
      quotation or fulfil an order. We share only what is needed for that purpose.
    </li>
    <li>Authorities, where required by law.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Some of these recipients may be located outside your country, including outside the European
    Economic Area or the United Kingdom. Where required, we rely on appropriate safeguards such as
    standard contractual clauses.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Enquiries that do not lead to an order are kept for up to 24 months and then deleted. Data
    relating to orders is kept for as long as required by applicable commercial and tax law.
    <Todo note="confirm retention periods" />
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you are, you may have the right to access, correct or delete your personal
    data, to restrict or object to its processing, and to data portability. To exercise any of these
    rights, email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. You also have the right to
    lodge a complaint with your local data protection authority.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    The website is served over HTTPS and form submissions are transmitted encrypted. Access to
    enquiry data is limited to people who need it to respond.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy. The date at the top of the page shows when it last changed.</p>
</LegalLayout>
